== History==
2016
*The Inferno Tower [[Cards|card]] was added with Clash Royale's game launch on 4/1/2016.
*On 2/2/2016, the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]], decreased the Inferno Tower's lifetime to 45 seconds (from 60 seconds) and increased the Inferno Tower's re-targeting time by 0.4 seconds.
*On 19/2/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (19/2/2016)|Balance Update]] decreased the Inferno Tower's hitpoints by 6% and lifetime to 40 seconds (from 45 seconds).
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], increased the {{Rarity|Rare}} card Level cap to 11 (from 10). The update also fixed the “range bug”, which decreased the Inferno Tower's range to 6 tiles (from 6.5 tiles), but its effective range is unchanged.
*On 4/7/2016, the [[Version History#Tournaments Update (4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], increased the Inferno Tower's hitpoints by 6%. It also gave [[Zap]] and [[Freeze]] the ability to reset the damage output.
*On 1/11/2016, the [[Version History#November 2016 Update (1/11/2016)|November 2016 Update]], decreased the Inferno Tower's hitpoints by 6%.
2017
*On 9/10/2017, the [[Version History#Epic%20Quests%20Update%20(9/10/2017)|Epic Quests Update]], fixed a bug where the Inferno Tower's damage did not reset after breaking a shield. This change was reverted on 11/10/2017, in a [[Version History#Maintenance%20Break%20(11/10/2017)|maintenance break]].
*On 12/12/2017, the [[Version History#Electrifying%20Update%20(12/12/2017)|Electrifying Update]], reverted the Inferno Tower to its state on 9/10/2017. More specifically, the Inferno Tower's damage would now reset after breaking a shield.
2018
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], fixed a bug where the Inferno Tower would occasionally stop shooting at the edge of its range.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Rare}} cards start at Level 3 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 11).
*On 5/11/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (5/11/2018)|Balance Update]], increased the Inferno Tower's hitpoints by 3%.
2019
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], decreased the Inferno Tower's lifetime to 30 seconds (from 40 seconds).
2021
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 3/2/2022, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(3/2/2022)|Balance Update]], decreased the Inferno Tower's re-targeting time by 0.4 seconds.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Inferno Tower from P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse to Spell Valley.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Inferno Tower's hitpoints by 0.05%.

